  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Quality/Value of Traded goods</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TradeMark Africa&apos;s Quality and Value of Traded Goods Portfolio works to remove standards and sanitary and phytosanitary compliance as a barrier to African exports, recognising that the ability to consistently meet international market requirements is the gateway to accessing higher-value regional and global trade opportunities, particularly as global buyers apply increasingly stringent environmental, social, and governance standards to production and supply chains. The Portfolio supports national standards bureaux to strengthen laboratory capacity, inspection and certification services, and conformity assessment infrastructure; works with governments to implement technical regulations consistent with WTO trade rules; facilitates harmonisation of standards frameworks at national, regional, and continental levels; pursues Mutual Recognition Agreements to build cross-border confidence in conformity assessment; and supports enterprises directly, with a focus on agricultural value chains and SMEs, to raise their compliance levels, access certification services, and connect to export markets. Across these interventions, the Portfolio&apos;s approach is to build durable national and regional quality infrastructure that enables African producers to trade on the basis of a single assessment, reducing duplication, lowering costs, and improving the predictability of cross-border trade.</narrative>
  </description>
